   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "The 1965 Supreme Court decision in <i>Griswold v. Connecticut</i> declared that",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1174555,
     "content_html": "laws against adultery were constitutional"
    },
    {
     "id": 1174556,
     "content_html": "married couples’ right to contraception was protected by a constitutional right to privacy"
    },
    {
     "id": 1174554,
     "content_html": "Margaret Sanger could not promote the use of contraceptives"
    },
    {
     "id": 1174553,
     "content_html": "state governments could legally restrict abortions"
    }
